l consecutive teachings on improper speech are reported by Ḥisda in Ukva’s name.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The Bavli leaves alternate transmitters, Rav Shimi bar Ukva or Mar Ukva, for the aggadah and his attendance on R. Shimon ben Pazi.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"Ukva quotes Shemuel in the treatment discussion.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"Ukva says Shemuel gave him a distinction between the two kinds of bread.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"Tavi bar Mari Tavi transmits Ukva in the name of Shemuel.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The two passages give separate received chains through Ukva to Shemuel, with Lil(i) bar Mammal and Mari bar Mar respectively.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The Hebrew locator already says end of 21b. The checked passage gives the Torah-locks exposition with this chain.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The same Shabbat passage explicitly has R. Yannai send to Ukva, and places bar Levai before him in another part.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"Levi is named alongside Shemuel’s father in the shared transmission, with an alternative assignment of each statement.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The exact Yerushalmi locator and relationship remain open. Berakhot explicitly gives a different comparison involving aggadah before R. Yehoshua ben Levi.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"Rav Yosef appears in the related attributions. The bare pointer does not establish which subpassage is intended.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The checked Ketubbot passage has Rav Anan address Mar Ukva as Mar.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The checked Bavli reads R. Akiva. Tosafot explicitly transmits one Mar Ukva emendation and another explanation retaining R. Akiva.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The reciprocal Akavya notice gives the exact Avodah Zarah passage. It supports Heilprin’s analogy without proving the emendation.","references":[],"urls":[]},{"text":"The digital Bavli read